EXT. LISTENING POST - NO MAN'S LAND - NIGHT - 1917

A shell crater, ankle-deep in water. Barbed wire above. Star shells pop on the horizon.

SGT. DRUMMOND, 30s, mud to the thighs, kneels at the lip with a rifle. LT. YUSUF ARSLAN, 20s, officer, binoculars round his neck, crouches beside him. A CAPTIVE, 20s, hands tied, kneels in the water at their feet, shivering in a grey tunic.

DRUMMOND
He's a boy.

ARSLAN
He's a prisoner.

DRUMMOND
He's a boy, sir.

ARSLAN
Ask his name.

DRUMMOND
(to the Captive)
Name?

The Captive says nothing. Drummond prods him with the rifle.

CAPTIVE
(thick accent)
Leopold.

DRUMMOND
Leopold what?

LEOPOLD
Just Leopold.

ARSLAN
Ask him where the machine gun is.

DRUMMOND
Where's the gun, Leopold?

LEOPOLD
No gun.

ARSLAN
He's lying.

A shell whistles overhead. The three duck. The crater erupts in mud. Leopold breaks for the wire, bound hands in front of him. Drummond lunges and catches his ankle. Arslan grabs his collar. All three go down in the water, thrashing.

Drummond pins him. Leopold goes limp. Arslan pulls Drummond off.

ARSLAN (CONT'D)
Enough.

They crouch, breathing. Leopold lies in the water, chest heaving.

LEOPOLD
(whispering)
My brother is in your trench. Joachim. He surrendered in March.

Drummond looks at Arslan.

DRUMMOND
Joachim? Big lad, cigarette burns?

LEOPOLD
Yes.

DRUMMOND
He's at the aid post. Alive.

Leopold closes his eyes. Arslan lowers the binoculars. Drummond cuts the rope on the boy's wrists.

Another shell. They duck again. Leopold, free, stays down.
